  "worked_solution": "First, we recall the following formula:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+2ay+{a}^{2}=(y+a{)}^{2}\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a perfect square in the parentheses that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+20y+{10}^{2} & = \\\\ {y}^{2}+2\\cdot 10y+{10}^{2} & = \\\\ (y+10{)}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({y}^{2}+20y+{10}^{2})+7 & = \\\\ (y+10{)}^{2}+7 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
